// Opening gap fade. The gap is this bar's open against the prior close, sized
// in units of the prior bar's ATR so the threshold means the same thing on a
// quiet instrument and a violent one. The fade is taken only when the bar has
// already closed back through its own open - the gap being large is not the
// signal, the gap failing is.
// REGIME: a session-bound instrument in a range, where an overnight gap is an
// imbalance rather than news. Do NOT fire on a breakaway gap: a gap that opens
// a new trend is the same shape on the open and the opposite trade, and no
// bar-level rule can tell the two apart. That is this rule's central risk and
// it is not solved here.
// INPUTS: open, high, low, close (series<float>). Requires a genuine session
// open, so it is meaningless on a continuously traded instrument where the
// open is just the previous close.
// CONDITIONS: gap at least 1.5 prior-bar ATRs, and a close on the wrong side
// of the open. Symmetric: the else arm is the down-gap mirror, and the two can
// never both be true because a gap cannot be up and down at once.
// INVALIDATION: a close beyond the gap extreme, which says the gap is being
// extended rather than filled. The host owns the stop; this rule proposes only.
// SHAPE: 1d; an outsized open that gives the whole move back by the close.
// NOT event_impulse_pullback_short: that is a macro-event rule on a five-second
// cadence, gated by a host event engine that has verified a scheduled release.
// This is a daily-bar rule with no event knowledge at all - if a red-folder
// release caused the gap, that rule should own it and this one should not fire.
// CALIBRATED ON: session-bound US equities, daily bars. 1.5 ATRs is a
// convention; because it is ATR-relative it travels across instruments, but it
// does not travel across cadences - on a 5m bar the "gap" is a single tick of
// slippage. The rule also assumes the open is executable, which is false in the
// first seconds of an auction.
strategy OpeningGapFade {

    param atr_window: int = 14
    param gap_atr: float = 1.5

    input open: series<float>
    input high: series<float>
    input low: series<float>
    input close: series<float>

    let gap = open - close[1]
    let threshold = ATR(high, low, close, atr_window)[1] * gap_atr

    every 1d {

        if gap >= threshold and close < open {

            sell(SPY, 0.55)

        } else {

            if gap <= -threshold and close > open {

                buy(SPY, 0.55)

            }

        }

    }

}
